---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const pipeline = [
  ['Long record', 'A source-led blog, report, signal, diagram, or system page carries the full context: source trail, what changed, what is missing, and the clear limit.'],
  ['Short note', 'The long record becomes a calm reader note: one idea, one reason it matters, one boundary, and one link back to the site.'],
  ['Platform draft', 'The same note is shaped for LinkedIn, X, dev.to, Telegram, or email without changing the underlying claim.'],
  ['Human post', 'Drafts are reviewed before posting. The system can prepare copy, but final public publishing stays with a person.'],
];

const formats = [
  {
    label: 'LinkedIn',
    body: 'Professional context, one strong opening, plain finance/compliance language, and the link preferably outside the main post when useful.',
  },
  {
    label: 'X',
    body: 'Short thread or single post: hook, source question, clear limit, and one route back to the full Bionic Banker record.',
  },
  {
    label: 'dev.to',
    body: 'Technical explainer from the same source record: system shape, boundary, example, and what remains human-reviewed.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Telegram / email',
    body: 'Reader-facing release note: New, why it matters, clear limit, and one link. No internal build logs.',
  },
];

const guardrails = [
  'No automated public posting until templates are stable and approval is explicit.',
  'No trading calls, copy-trade instructions, KYC decisions, SAR filings, or wallet-control claims.',
  'No private prompts, internal paths, employer data, customer data, or agent build logs.',
  'No claim should grow larger when it moves from blog to social format.',
  'Each short post should point back to a source-led Bionic Banker page, report, or article.',
];

const draftShape = [
  ['Source page', 'The Bionic Banker route that carries the full record.'],
  ['Reader idea', 'The one useful idea the post should preserve.'],
  ['Why it matters', 'The finance, AI, risk, or compliance question a reader can inspect.'],
  ['Clear limit', 'What the record cannot prove, decide, approve, or execute.'],
  ['Channel draft', 'The platform-specific draft text.'],
  ['Approval status', 'Draft only, needs review, approved, or posted by human.'],
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Content System" description="Bionic Banker content system: turn source-led website records into shorter platform drafts without changing the claim, removing limits, or auto-posting.">
  <main class="content-system-shell">
    <section class="content-hero">
      <div class="content-kicker">Bionic Banker Content System</div>
      <h1>One source record. Many public formats. Same limits.</h1>
      <p>The website stays the source of truth. A blog, report, signal, or system page carries the full record first. Shorter posts for LinkedIn, X, dev.to, Telegram, or email are drafted from that record so the message stays consistent.</p>
      <div class="content-actions">
        <a href="/articles">Read articles</a>
        <a href="/updates">Update promise</a>
        <a href="/context-engine">Context Engine</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section thesis-card">
      <span>Operating rule</span>
      <h2>Publish the full record first. Draft distribution second.</h2>
      <p>Bionic Banker should not invent disconnected social posts. The sequence is: build the source-led page, compress the useful idea, adapt it to each channel, keep the clear limit, and let a human decide when it goes public.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <span>Pipeline</span>
      <h2>From website record to public draft.</h2>
      <div class="pipeline-grid">
        {pipeline.map(([label, body], index) => (
          <article>
            <strong>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')} · {label}</strong>
            <p>{body}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section split">
      <div>
        <span>Platform formats</span>
        <h2>Different shape, same claim.</h2>
        <p>Each channel can sound native without changing the source meaning. The blog can hold the full context and diagrams; the short post should carry only the cleanest reader idea and link back.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="format-grid">
        {formats.map((item) => (
          <article>
            <strong>{item.label}</strong>
            <p>{item.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section split">
      <div>
        <span>Draft contract</span>
        <h2>Automation can prepare the packet, not publish it by default.</h2>
        <p>The safe automation target is a draft packet. It should show the source page, target channel, draft text, clear limit, and approval status before anything is posted.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="draft-card">
        <strong>Required draft packet</strong>
        <ul>
          {draftShape.map(([label, body]) => <li><b>{label}:</b> {body}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <span>Guardrails</span>
      <h2>Distribution should not make the claim bigger.</h2>
      <ul class="guard-list">
        {guardrails.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section sample-card">
      <span>Example shape</span>
      <h2>Reader-facing social draft from a Bionic Banker page.</h2>
      <p><b>Source page:</b> /context-engine/</p>
      <p><b>Post idea:</b> In finance and AI, the useful layer is not a bigger prompt. It is the record around the prompt: source trail, missing context, clear limit, and human next step.</p>
      <p><b>Clear limit:</b> This does not approve KYC, file reports, move funds, accuse a wallet, or tell readers what to trade.</p>
      <p><b>Status:</b> Draft only until reviewed and posted by a human.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .content-system-shell { max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 6rem 1.25rem 4rem; color: var(--text); }
  .content-hero, .content-section { border: 1px solid rgba(31,160,104,.16); background: rgba(3,16,8,.92); border-radius: 28px; padding: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 3rem); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; box-shadow: 0 24px 80px rgba(0,0,0,.28); }
  .content-kicker, .content-section > span { color: #1fa068; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .16em; font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 900; }
  .content-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5.4vw, 4.8rem); line-height: .96; margin: .75rem 0 1rem; max-width: 960px; }
  .content-hero p, .content-section p, .content-section li { color: #b0b0b8; line-height: 1.72; font-size: 1.02rem; }
  .content-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .content-actions a { text-decoration: none; border-radius: 999px; padding: .82rem 1.05rem; border: 1px solid rgba(31,160,104,.24); color: var(--text); font-weight: 850; }
  .content-actions a:first-child { background: #1fa068; color: #010302; border: 0; }
  .pipeline-grid, .format-grid { display: grid; gap: .85rem; }
  .pipeline-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); margin-top: 1rem; }
  .pipeline-grid article, .format-grid article, .draft-card, .sample-card { border: 1px solid rgba(31,160,104,.14); border-radius: 18px; background: rgba(31,160,104,.055); padding: 1rem; }
  .pipeline-grid strong, .format-grid strong, .draft-card strong { display: block; color: #f4f7f1; margin-bottom: .45rem; }
  .split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) minmax(280px,.95fr); gap: 1rem; align-items: start; }
  .draft-card ul, .guard-list { margin: 1rem 0 0 1.25rem; }
  .draft-card li, .guard-list li { margin-bottom: .6rem; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .split { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .content-system-shell { padding-top: 4.5rem; } }
</style>
